+# Rane One (MK1) mapping reference
+
+What each physical control does in Mixxx 2.5.6 with `mapping/Rane-One.midi.xml` + `mapping/Rane-One-scripts.js`
+(status M6, 2026-10-26). Sources: the mapping itself, [`docs/decisions.md`](decisions.md) D27–D35, and
+[`reference/rane-one-mk1-controls.csv`](../reference/rane-one-mk1-controls.csv) for the MIDI rows.
+
+- **The platters are not wired yet (M7).** Platter touch/turn (CC 6 + pitch bend, ch 1/2) is only counted; Mixxx plays
+  by its own clock. The pitch fader sets Mixxx's rate to match the motor (D27), but nothing is sent to the motor.
+- **Nothing is sent to the controller**: no LEDs, no display, no motor.
+- **UNVERIFIED** = the controls CSV gives the row `mk2` or `unknown` confidence: the name comes from the MK2 djay map
+  or an inference, no capture proves it. Rows without it name a capture in the CSV's `evidence` column.
+- MIDI column: status byte `0x9n` is note-on, `0xBn` control change, `0xEn` pitch bend, channel `n+1`. Buttons also
+  send note-off (`0x8n`) on release. **Deck 2 is the same row on channel 2 (deck notes) and 6 (pad-section notes)**,
+  except where a row says otherwise. Notes are decimal.
+- Deck buttons that send their own note with Shift are listed as two rows; Play and the pitch bends send the same note
+  with or without Shift, so one row holds both.
+- Pots (knobs, faders) have **soft takeover**: after a Mixxx-side change they do nothing until the physical control
+  passes the on-screen value.
+- Round 2/3 hardware steps that will turn UNVERIFIED rows into verified ones: [`HARDWARE-TESTS.md`](../HARDWARE-TESTS.md).
+
+## Deck (deck 1 shown; `[Channel1]`, deck 2 `[Channel2]`)
+
+| Physical control | MIDI | Mixxx control | |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Play | `0x90` ch 1 #0 | `play` (toggle) | |
+| Shift+Play | same note | `play` (toggle: Play, not reverse, D31) | |
+| Cue | `0x90` ch 1 #1 | Components `CueButton` (`cue_default`) | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+Cue | `0x90` ch 1 #5 | `start` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Sync | `0x90` ch 1 #2 | Components `SyncButton`: tap `beatsync`, hold `sync_enabled` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+Sync | `0x90` ch 1 #3 | `sync_enabled` = 0 | UNVERIFIED |
+| Load | `0x90` ch 1 #6 | `LoadSelectedTrack` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+Load | `0x90` ch 1 #8 | `LoadSelectedTrack` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Back | `0x90` ch 1 #7 | `[Library],MoveFocusBackward` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+Back | `0x90` ch 1 #18 | `[Skin],show_maximized_library` (toggle) | UNVERIFIED |
+| Library encoder (turn) | `0xB0` ch 1 #0, relative 63/65 | `[Library],MoveVertical` ±1 per tick (which way 65 scrolls is unconfirmed) | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+library encoder | `0xB1` ch 2 #1 (seen on deck 2 only) | `[Library],MoveVertical` ±10 per tick | UNVERIFIED |
+| Pitch bend + | `0x90` ch 1 #11 | `rate_temp_up` while held | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+pitch bend + | same note | `rate_temp_up_small` while held | UNVERIFIED |
+| Pitch bend − | `0x90` ch 1 #12 | `rate_temp_down` while held | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+pitch bend − | same note | `rate_temp_down_small` while held | UNVERIFIED |
+| Range | `0x90` ch 1 #43 | none (counted; it does not change the motor, D27) | |
+| Shift+Range | `0x90` ch 1 #13 | `keylock` (toggle) | |
+| Reverse (deck pad) | `0x90` ch 1 #16 | `reverse` (toggle) | UNVERIFIED (note 16 is the MK2's name; HARDWARE-TESTS round 2 step 4) |
+| Shift+Reverse | `0x90` ch 1 #17 | `reverseroll` (censor) while held; the deck's Reverse and Slip are restored after | UNVERIFIED |
+| Pitch fader | `0xB0` ch 1 #9 (MSB) + #41 (LSB), 14 bit | `rate`, set so Mixxx plays at 0.5× (bottom) / 1× (centre) / 1.5× (top) like the motor, whatever `rateRange` is; the mapping sets `rateRange` 0.5 at init (D27) | |
+| Strip search | `0xB0` ch 1 #43 (MSB) + #75 (LSB), 14 bit | `playposition`; only while the deck is stopped or Shift is held (D34) | |
+| Stop Time knob | `0xB0` ch 1 #72 | none: stored for M7 (counted) | |
+| Platter turn / touch | `0xB0` ch 1 #6 + `0xE0` ch 1 | none until M7 (counted) | |
+| Slip | `0x94` ch 5 #9 | `slip_enabled` (toggle) | |
+| Shift+Slip | `0x94` ch 5 #10 | none: flips the One's motor-off state kept for M7 (counted) | |
+| Pad parameter ◂ | `0x94` ch 5 #40 | `beatjump_backward` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Pad parameter ▸ | `0x94` ch 5 #41 | `beatjump_forward` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+pad parameter ◂ | `0x94` ch 5 #42 | `beatjump_size` × ½ (1/32 … 512 beats) | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+pad parameter ▸ | `0x94` ch 5 #43 | `beatjump_size` × 2 | UNVERIFIED |
+| Loop halve | `0x94` ch 5 #52 | `loop_halve` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Loop double | `0x94` ch 5 #53 | `loop_double` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+loop halve | `0x94` ch 5 #54 | `loop_in` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+loop double | `0x94` ch 5 #55 | `loop_out` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Auto loop | `0x94` ch 5 #63 | `reloop_toggle` if a loop is on, else `beatloop_activate` | UNVERIFIED |
+| Shift+auto loop | `0x94` ch 5 #65 | `reloop_toggle` | UNVERIFIED |
+
+## Pads and pad modes (per deck; Hot Cue at start)
+
+Pad *i* (1–8) sends note 19 + *i* on ch 5 (deck 1) / 6 (deck 2), and 27 + *i* with Shift. The pads themselves are
+verified (`capture`); the mode names and notes are not. Every target is momentary: 1 while the pad is held. Each mode
+note sends the same note with Shift and selects the same mode.
+
+| Mode (MIDI: `0x94` ch 5 note) | Pad *i* (notes 20–27) | Shift+pad *i* (notes 28–35) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Hot Cue (#0) UNVERIFIED | `hotcue_i_activate` | `hotcue_i_clear` |
+| Saved Loop (#13) UNVERIFIED | `hotcue_(i+8)_activate` (second bank) | `hotcue_(i+8)_clear` |
+| Roll (#7) UNVERIFIED | `beatlooproll_X_activate`, X = 1/16, 1/8, 1/4, 1/2, 1, 2, 4, 8 | `beatloop_X_toggle` |
+| Sampler (#11) UNVERIFIED | `[Sampler i],cue_gotoandplay` (either deck's pad) | `[Sampler i],cue_gotoandstop` |
+| Beat Jump, the One's "Stems" (#12) UNVERIFIED | pads 1–4 `beatjump_1/2/4/8_backward`, pads 5–8 `beatjump_1/2/4/8_forward` | the same at 4× (4/8/16/32) |
+
+A Sampler pad past `[App],num_samplers` is counted, not mapped. A Roll pad restores the deck's Slip after it ends.
+
+## Mixer
+
+Channel 1 on ch 1, channel 2 on ch 2 (same numbers). All rows UNVERIFIED unless noted.
+
+| Physical control | MIDI | Mixxx control |
+|---|---|---|
+| Channel trim | `0xB0` ch 1 #22 | `[Channel1],pregain` |
+| EQ high | `0xB0` ch 1 #23 | `[EqualizerRack1_[Channel1]_Effect1],parameter3` |
+| EQ mid | `0xB0` ch 1 #24 | `…,parameter2` |
+| EQ low | `0xB0` ch 1 #25 | `…,parameter1` |
+| Filter | `0xB0` ch 1 #26 | `[QuickEffectRack1_[Channel1]],super1` |
+| Headphone cue | `0x90` ch 1 #27 (reported state: value >0 on, 0 off) | `[Channel1],pfl` |
+| Channel fader | `0xB0` ch 1 #28 | `[Channel1],volume` (starts at 0 until the first move, D35) |
+| Crossfader | `0xBF` ch 16 #8 | `[Master],crossfader` |
+| Front-panel knob A | `0xB0` ch 15 #35 | `[Master],headMix` (which knob is which is unconfirmed) |
+| Front-panel knob B | `0xB0` ch 15 #36 | `[Master],headGain` |
+| Motor torque switch (rear) | `0xB0` ch 15 #96 | none: stored for M7 (counted). Verified (`capture`) |
+
+## FX section
+
+| Physical control | MIDI | Mixxx control |
+|---|---|---|
+| FX paddle, deck 1 | `0x98` ch 9 #16 (127 up/locked, 0 down) | `[EffectRack1_EffectUnit1],group_[Channel1]_enable` = paddle state |
+| FX paddle, deck 2 | `0x99` ch 10 #16 | `[EffectRack1_EffectUnit2],group_[Channel2]_enable` |
+| FX 1–3 | `0x98` ch 9 #0–2 (value 0, sent with each paddle change) | none (counted) |
+| FX 4–6 | `0x99` ch 10 #3–5 | none (counted) |
+| Tap | `0x9F` ch 16 #4 | `bpm_tap` on the deck whose paddle is on (deck 1 if both; counted if none) |
+| Depth knob | `0xBF` ch 16 #4 | `mix` of both effect units. The 0 the One sends with each paddle-on is held and dropped (D32) |
+| Beat knob (endless) | `0xBF` ch 16 #3, relative 63/65. Verified (`capture`) | `super1` of both effect units, ±1/32 per tick |
+
+All FX rows except the beat knob are UNVERIFIED. The FX section was not recorded with Shift (HARDWARE-TESTS round 2
+step 1): nothing is mapped on that layer.
+
+## Shift layer
+
+| Physical control | MIDI | What it does |
+|---|---|---|
+| Shift | `0x9F` ch 16 #50. Verified (`capture`) | Held state in `RaneOne.shifted`. Most buttons send their own Shift note and ignore it; the same-note buttons (Play, pitch bends) and the strip (D34) read it |
+
+Every Shift variant of a control is in its own table above.
