+## Script structure
+
+`mapping/Rane-One.midi.xml` `<scriptfiles>`, in order: `midi-components-0.0.js` (Mixxx's own copy: not in
+`mapping/`, Mixxx finds it in its system controllers directory; `common-controller-scripts.js` Mixxx loads by
+itself), `rane-one-platter.js`, `Rane-One-scripts.js` (prefix `RaneOne`). `<info><description>` drops "M1
+skeleton". No `<outputs>`.
+
+`mapping/Rane-One-scripts.js` (plain script, `var` at top level only for `RaneOne`; ES2015 inside, as
+midi-components-0.0.js itself uses `const`):
+- **`RaneOne.guard(name, fn)`** stays as it is. Every function Mixxx calls is either guarded or a component's
+  `input`/`inputMSB`/`inputLSB`, and **every component input is guarded too**: after `init` builds the
+  containers, `RaneOne.guardInputs(root)` walks them (`forEachComponent`, recursive) and wraps each input once
+  (marked `guarded`), named by its path (`deck1.cue.input`). Inputs only change on `shift()` (Components'
+  `SyncButton`, `SamplerButton` swap `input`), so `RaneOne.shift` re-runs `guardInputs` on what it shifted. A
+  thrown handler then logs one warning and the message is dropped (CLAUDE.md: handlers never throw).
+- **`RaneOne.Deck(n)`** extends `components.Deck([n])` (`[Channel1]`/`[Channel2]`). Two instances,
+  `RaneOne.deck1` and `RaneOne.deck2`, own every row on channel n (1/2) and n + 4 (5/6): transport, library
+  buttons, pitch fader, strip, Stop Time store, pads, pad modes, Slip, pad parameter and loop buttons, and the
+  platter placeholder `deckN.platter` (an `input` that only counts, until M7). Members by the table; mode state
+  in `deckN.padMode.mode` (one `RaneOne.PadMode` for the five mode notes; a mode note selects the same mode with
+  Shift, so it ignores Shift and is not in `sameNote`); the pads are `deckN.pads.pad1..8`, each a `RaneOne.Pad`
+  that reads the mode at the press (M6-05); `deckN.sameNote` holds Play and the pitch bend buttons.
+- **`RaneOne.Mixer()`** (`RaneOne.mixer`): per channel `trim`, `eqHigh`, `eqMid`, `eqLow`, `filter`, `pfl`,
+  `volume` (in `mixer.channel1`/`channel2`), plus `crossfader`, `headMix`, `headGain`, the `torque` store. The
+  mixer rows are on the deck channels but belong here: Mixxx's mixer is not a deck.
+- **`RaneOne.Fx()`** (`RaneOne.fx`): `paddle1`, `paddle2`, `fxState` (the FX1–6 no-op), `depth`, `beat`, `tap`,
+  by D32. Not `components.EffectUnit`: the MK1's FX buttons send nothing usable (census § FX section) and the
+  One's FX section is shared by both decks, which EffectUnit doesn't model.
+- **Shift: note 50 ch 16** → `RaneOne.shift.input`: on press `deck1.sameNote.shift()`, `deck2.sameNote.shift()`,
+  `fx.shift()` and `RaneOne.shifted = true` (read by the strip, D34); on release the same with `unshift()`. The
+  layered components never see it.
+- **Pitch fader (CC 9 MSB, CC 41 LSB, channel n).** Take 23: CC 9 comes first in every pair and both halves share
+  one `t_us` in 4,467 of 4,476 (census § Census). Rule: **CC 9 alone applies `(MSB << 7) + 64`** (within 64 steps,
+  1/256 of the travel, of any LSB), **CC 41 then applies `(MSB << 7) | LSB`** exactly; a CC 41 before any CC 9 is
+  dropped (the tail of a pair whose MSB came before the port opened; M6-04 review). Value v → `rate = rate_dir × (motorRatioFromFader(v) − 1) / rateRange`, clamped to
+  ±1, with `motorRatioFromFader` from `RaneOnePlatter` (0 = 0.5×, 8192 = 1×, 16383 = 1.5×) and `rate_dir`,
+  `rateRange` read live (D27, M5-06's decision: the motor runs 1 ± 0.5× whatever Range says). `init` sets `rateRange` 0.5 on both channels; a `rateRange` under 0.5 seen at a
+  fader move logs once (D27). No soft takeover; until the deck's first CC 9/41, `rate` is left alone (D27).
+- **Strip (CC 43 MSB, CC 75 LSB):** the same MSB-first rule, into `playposition` = v / 16383, applied only while
+  the deck's `play` is 0 or `RaneOne.shifted` (D34).
+- **Encoders** (CC 0/1 on channels 1/2, CC 3 ch 16) are relative: delta = value − 64 (63 → −1, 65 → +1).
+- **Debug log (M6-06):** `RaneOne.DEBUG` (false in the repo). When true, `init` makes one `engine.makeConnection`
+  per (group, key) the mapping can change and logs `RaneOne: <group>,<key> = <value>` on each change: Mixxx's
+  own report of what moved, which M6-07 greps. `tools/install-mapping --debug` sets it true in the dev-profile copy
+  only (it rewrites the one `RaneOne.DEBUG = false;` line and refuses if that line isn't there exactly once;
+  bad-argument cases in `tests/tools-usage.test.mjs`, per Gotchas).
+- **XML naming:** every `<key>` is `RaneOne.<container>.<member>.input` (`RaneOne.deck1.play.input`,
+  `RaneOne.deck1.pads.pad3.input`, `RaneOne.mixer.channel1.eqHigh.input`, `RaneOne.fx.depth.input`,
+  `RaneOne.shift.input`, `RaneOne.noop`); `inputMSB`/`inputLSB` for the 14-bit pairs. **Every note gets two
+  entries, 0x9n and 0x8n, with the same key:** the One releases buttons with real note-offs (0x8n: 414 in takes
+  02–06 and 25–28) and reports states as 0x9n with value 0 (78, the FX state burst and the paddle-off), and
+  Mixxx binds by exact status byte. Every entry has
+  `<status>`, `<midino>`, `<options><script-binding/></options>` and a comment naming the controls-CSV row
+  (`UNVERIFIED` when `mk2`/`unknown`). Mixxx calls `(<key>)(channel, control, value, status, group)`, so the
+  object before the last dot is `this`, resolved at each call: the harness calls it the same way.
+- **Sends nothing:** no component gets a `midi` option (Components' `send` returns without one), and the existing
+  tests (no `midi.send`, no read of the `midi` object) keep holding with Components loaded.
+
+## Test harness
+
+`tests/helpers/fake-mixxx.mjs` (M6-02), zero dependencies (D5):
+- **Library location:** `$(flatpak info --show-location org.mixxx.Mixxx)/files/share/mixxx/controllers/`
+  (`spawnSync`, 5 s timeout), overridable with `RANE_MIXXX_CONTROLLERS` for a test. When the directory or
+  `midi-components-0.0.js` is missing, `loadMapping()` returns `{ skip: "<why>" }` and each test file passes it
+  to `test(name, { skip })`: an explicit skip with the reason, never a failure. The file header says so.
+- **Load:** a `vm` context; then `common-controller-scripts.js` (Mixxx loads it for every mapping), then each
+  `<file>` of the XML's `<scriptfiles>` in order, from `mapping/` if it is there, else from the Mixxx directory.
+  Then `RaneOne.init("Midi Through Port-0", false)`.
+- **Fake `engine`:** a value store keyed `group,key` (unset reads 0; `getParameter`/`setParameter` the same store
+  in 0–1, with `rateRange` 0.5 and `rate_dir` 1 preset), recording every `setValue`/`setParameter` as
+  `[group, key, value]` and every `softTakeover`/`softTakeoverIgnoreNextValue` call; `makeConnection` returns an
+  object with `disconnect`, `trigger`, and the fake fires the callbacks on set (for the debug log);
+  `beginTimer`/`stopTimer` keep timers the test runs with `harness.tick(ms)`; `getSetting` returns undefined
+  (defaults apply); `isScratching` false. A test can make any method throw (`harness.failNext(name)`).
+- **Fake `midi`:** `sendShortMsg` and `sendSysexMsg` throw, and the harness counts reads of `midi.*`
+  (expected 0). Fake `script` comes from the real `common-controller-scripts.js`; `console.log/warn` recorded.
+- **Dispatch:** the XML's `<control>` entries become a table keyed by (status high nibble, channel, number). A
+  JSONL record (capture format: `bytes`, `type`, `ch`, `d1`, `d2`) or `[status, d1, d2]` is looked up and called
+  as Mixxx does: `vm.runInContext("(" + key + ")")`'s owner and function, `fn.call(owner, channel - 1, d1, d2,
+  status, group)`. The lookup is by the exact status byte, as Mixxx's is: a note-off (0x8n) needs its own
+  entry. A pitch bend (0xEn) is looked up by its status alone (M6-06): its first byte is the value's LSB, and
+  Mixxx's own pitch bend fader mappings have one entry with no `<midino>` (Icon-iControls, MVave-SMC-Mixer);
+  Mixxx's exact rule is UNVERIFIED, for M7. Messages with no entry go to `harness.unhandled` (with their channel and number); exceptions that escape
+  a handler go to `harness.thrown` (expected empty: the guard is the system under test).
+- **Capture replays:** `harness.replay(file)` dispatches every channel message of a census take in order (no
+  timing; timers advanced by the take's `t_us` gaps) and returns `{ sent, unhandled, thrown, sets }`.
+- **Tests per feature:** M6-02 `mapping-harness.test.mjs` (the fake itself, Button/Pot inside it, the skip);
+  M6-03 `mapping-deck.test.mjs`; M6-04 `mapping-mixer.test.mjs`; M6-05 `mapping-pads.test.mjs`; M6-06
+  `mapping-fx.test.mjs` and the census-replay table. Each asserts on lengths and first mismatches, not
+  `deepEqual` over whole recordings.
+- **Existing tests that change (M6-02):** `tests/mapping-xml.test.mjs` "the script list is rane-one-platter.js
+  then Rane-One-scripts.js" becomes the three-file list (midi-components-0.0.js need not be in `mapping/`); its
+  `load()` with the hostile `engine` proxy loads Components too (from the harness's directory, skipping when
+  absent) so "no RaneOne handler can throw" and "touches the midi object" walk the built containers after
+  `init`.
+
+## Replay check
+
+M6-07, in Michael's desktop session (`WAYLAND_DISPLAY` set; if it is empty, the steps are written down as skipped
+with that reason, not faked). Nothing reaches the One: `tools/replay` refuses any port the One can reach, and
+`tools/mixxx-dev start` refuses a Midi Through subscribed to a Rane client.
+
+```sh
+tools/install-mapping --debug            # mapping/ → dev-profile/controllers/, RaneOne.DEBUG = true in the copy
+tools/mixxx-dev start                    # --controller-debug --controller-abort-on-warning; quote its route check
+tools/mixxx-dev log 200 | grep -E 'RaneOne: init|[Ww]arning|Critical'
+for t in 02-census-mixer 03-census-d1-controls 04-census-d1-pads 05-census-d2-controls \
+         06-census-d2-pads 27-census-d1-pads-shift 28-census-d2-pads-shift; do
+  n0=$(wc -l < ~/.var/app/org.mixxx.Mixxx/dev-profile/mixxx.log)
+  tools/replay --to-port 'Midi Through' --speed 4 captures/2026-10-23-census/$t.jsonl   # --speed 1 if lines drop
+  tail -n +$((n0 + 1)) ~/.var/app/org.mixxx.Mixxx/dev-profile/mixxx.log > /tmp/harness/rane-one-mixxx/rane-one-mixxx-2026-10-24/$t.log
+  grep -oE 'RaneOne: \[[^,]*\],[A-Za-z0-9_.]+' /tmp/harness/rane-one-mixxx/rane-one-mixxx-2026-10-24/$t.log | sort -u | wc -l
+done
+tools/mixxx-dev stop && tools/mixxx-dev status    # prints: stopped
+```
+
+**Pass:** the log has `RaneOne: init` and no warning or critical line from the controller (a mapping warning
+aborts Mixxx anyway); every replay exits 0; each take's log has `RaneOne: <group>,<key> = …` lines for the controls
+the harness replay (M6-06) says it changes, and the controls with no line are only the counted no-op rows and the
+platter (any other gap is a fail and names its row); Mixxx is stopped and its route check named the mixxx-dev null
+sink only. Results go to `.harness/runs/rane-one-mixxx-2026-10-24/checks/M6-replay.md` (one table per take:
+messages sent, distinct controls changed, ten sample lines, rows with no line). Also checked there (D27's open
+items): `rate_ratio` against `1 + rate × rateRange × rate_dir` at three fader values, and whether applying
+Preferences resets `rateRange`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- **The platters (M7).** CC 6 and the pitch bend on channels 1 and 2 are routed to `RaneOne.deck1.platter.input`
+  and `RaneOne.deck2.platter.input`, which only count messages (a comment says M7 replaces them). No scratching,
+  no `engine.scratch*`, no hybrid playback, no `<settings>` (D25's are M7's).
+- **Any output:** no `midi.send*` anywhere, no `<outputs>`, no LEDs, no motor or display messages (CLAUDE.md, D13
+  rules; `grep -c 'midi.send' mapping/Rane-One-scripts.js` prints 0).
+- **Transport and the motor agreeing.** Play, Cue, Shift+Cue, Sync, the pitch bend buttons, Reverse and the motor-off
+  mode change Mixxx's play state or rate while the One runs its motor by itself. M6 maps them as Mixxx does;
+  whether Mixxx must follow or ignore them while the motor turns (Cue while playing stops Mixxx; does it stop the
+  motor?) is M7's, with round 2 step 2.
+- **The power-on dump's extra rows** (20 state CCs and note 65 ch 16 with no census row): Mixxx ignores a message
+  with no `<control>`, so the dump is harmless; mapping them waits for their names (round 2).
+- **No encoder press** is in the census (no row): if the One's browse knobs push, round 2 step 9 finds it.
+- 45 rpm (D26), Mixxx C++ changes, ESLint against Mixxx's config (M9).
+
